      "notes": "All claims are appropriately tiered and supported by their quoted evidence. The E13 claim is sourced via vertexaisearch (routing to health.org.uk/Health Foundation) \u2014 an advocacy/think-tank source \u2014 and is labelled as supporting a 'measurable' claim; this is a mild concern since it is a single source and the tier should arguably be 'projected', but the Health Foundation is a credible body and the claim is hedged as 'highlights' rather than stated as established fact, so this is a warning rather than blocking. The mixed direction is genuinely supported by claims on both sides (revenue uplift vs deterrence/workforce effects), so false_balance does not apply. The magnitude of 'moderate' is defensible given the scale of projected revenue offset against projected harms. No party-blind or lever-leakage issues detected."
